  "name": "The Sepulcher Bridge",
  "description": "One stone bridge over the Grey Water, and nothing else for a day's march either way. The south bank rises in two ridges that close on a gated wall across the bridgehead, so whatever crosses the bridge has to cross it under the bows on both ridges and then break the gate. The north bank is barrows and dead wood, and that is where the dead come from.",
